omotion; the landed change promotes **13**. `reducer`\nis EXCLUDED. Its single un-annotated def is `reducer._filters.match_predicate(value)`, whose\ntype depends on the `op` argument (scalar / iterable / (lo,hi) pair). `value: object` was\ntried and produced 7 real mypy errors in the body; `value: Any` would satisfy tier 1 while\nbuying neither driver — the exact failure mode cc77 documents. Papering over it would have\nviolated the plan's own no-new-Any acceptance criterion, so it was filed instead:\nlegged-tenuous-bonobo (d893-e003-0539-47fc), linked discovered_from.\n\nThe larger residue (llm 293 / _commands 146 / _engine 134 untyped defs, ~390 explicit Any) is\nfiled as acute-agitable-xiphosuran (003c-2dd2-203a-4725), also linked discovered_from.\n\nMeasured result: tier 1 goes 2 -> 13 packages; tier 2 (`disallow_any_explicit`, new) covers\n`rebar._cli.*` and `rebar._snapshot.*`. Repo-wide explicit-Any count unchanged (no new Any\nintroduced by the 36 annotations).","timestamp":1786649327374035001}],"created_at":1785479760721669001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9d6eb8ab-731d-4bf3-9bce-97620d874e6d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8"},{"link_uuid":"d331b329-c360-440b-8c79-9bb7639adea1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dbf9-3fc8-625d-4730"},{"link_uuid":"f6117b42-6ae6-42eb-bb6d-1069320664a3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ae1b-b2a0-a080-4b4e"},{"link_uuid":"62276737-8d4b-4e90-b669-5bd0bc8c20bf","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9efe-8e88-70b3-4984"},{"link_uuid":"881dea18-a1a0-4f54-8ec0-5c9213a9ea3e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c4c-a2d9-1604-4fe1"}],"description":"# Ratchet `Any` and loose typing repo-wide (re-scoped against current main)\n\n## Premise re-validated on main @ ea6ee67e6a (measured, not assumed)\n\nThe original description's baseline is stale. Re-measured today with\n`mypy src/rebar/<pkg> --disallow-untyped-defs` (repo settings) and\n`--disallow-any-explicit`:\n\n| package | untyped-def errors | +explicit-Any errors |\n|---|---|---|\n| attest, graph, grounding, metrics | 0 | 2 / 15 / 116 / 76 |\n| _snapshot, _store, reducer | 1 | 0 / 17 / 5 |\n| schemas | 2 | 5 |\n| opcert_service, review_bot | 3 | 1 / 42 |\n| _io, _engine_support | 4 | 8 / 7 |\n| audit | 7 | 15 |\n| _cli | 11 | 0 |\n| _engine | 134 | large |\n| _commands | 146 | large |\n| llm | 293 | large |\n\nTwo facts change the scope:\n\n1. Sibling `abasic-doddering-harrier` (9efe) annotated `attest` and **explicitly deferred\n   the one-line ratchet promotion to this ticket**; `metrics` is *also* already clean and\n   was never promoted. Both flips are free today.\n2. The gap between \"already in the ratchet\" (`rebar.graph.*`, `rebar.grounding.*` in\n   `pyproject.toml`) and \"already clean\" is **12 packages**, and 10 of those are within\n   **37 trivial annotations** total. The genuinely hard residue is only\n   `llm` / `_commands` / `_engine` (573 untyped defs, ~389 explicit `Any`).\n\nSo the ticket's own AC #2 (\"extend the ratchet to constrain `Any`\") is achievable **with\nmypy's own `disallow_any_explicit`** rather than a bespoke counter: `_cli` and `_snapshot`\nmeasure at **zero** explicit-`Any` errors, so they can carry both flags as the worked\nexample. Reducing `Any` in `llm`/`_engine` and converting the reconciler transport port\nend-to-end are NOT trivially small and are split out (below), not attempted here.\n\n## Plan\n\n**A. Annotate the 37 remaining untyped defs (annotations only, no behaviour change, no new `Any`).**\nEvery one is a missing return type or an un-annotated `repo_root=None` / `args` / callback\nparameter:\n- `rebar._snapshot.cache.open_in_snapshot`, `rebar._store.hlc._hlc_lock`,\n  `rebar.reducer._filters.match_predicate` (the `value` param).\n- `rebar.schemas.registry`, `rebar.schemas.validator`.\n- `rebar.opcert_service.jobs.run_job` / `_dispatch_completion` / `_dispatch_plan_review`\n  (the `fn` callbacks -> `Callable[...]`).\n- `rebar.review_bot.adapter._resolve_reviewed_head` / `_assert_reviewed_tree` /\n  `code_review_decision` (`repo_root`).\n- `rebar._io.import_ndjson.import_tickets`, `rebar._io.export_ndjson.export_tickets`,\n  `rebar._io._cli.export_cli` / `import_cli` (`repo_root`).\n- `rebar._engine_support.output._resolve_profile` / `error_envelope`,\n  `rebar._engine_support.bridge_fsck._load_classify` (-> `ModuleType`).\n- `rebar.audit.read.plan_review_health` / `_completion_attestation` /\n  `_completion_sidecar_record` / `_related_code_reviews` / `audit_trail` / `rebar_show`,\n  `rebar.audit.server._render_ticket` (all `repo_root`).\n- `rebar._cli._llm_eval_commands._prompt_eval` / `_criteria_eval` / `_pct` / `_llm_setup`,\n  `rebar._cli._workflow_commands._workflow_{edit,show,run,read,new,validate}`,\n  `rebar._cli._bridge_commands._ref_lock_module` (`args` -> `argparse.Namespace`).\n\nAll 14 touched files are 127-684 LOC; none is near the 800 cap, and no file gains more\nthan ~11 lines. `llm/pass1.py` and `_lib_writes.py` are NOT touched.\n\n**B. Promote every now-clean package in `pyproject.toml`** into the existing\n`[[tool.mypy.overrides]]` `disallow_untyped_defs` block: `rebar.attest.*`,\n`rebar.metrics.*`, `rebar._snapshot.*`, `rebar._store.*`, `rebar.reducer.*`,\n`rebar.schemas.*`, `rebar.opcert_service.*`, `rebar.review_bot.*`, `rebar._io.*`,\n`rebar._engine_support.*`, `rebar.audit.*`, `rebar._cli.*` (2 -> 14 packages).\n\n**C. Extend the ratchet to constrain `Any`** — a SECOND override block with\n`disallow_any_explicit = true` for the packages measured clean under it\n(`rebar._cli.*`, `rebar._snapshot.*`), re-verified after step A. This is the mechanism the\nticket asks for, built from existing machinery, not a parallel one.\n\n**D. Guard it, shrink-only, in `tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py`.** Grow\n`_RATCHET_BASELINE` to the 14 promoted packages, and add `_ANY_RATCHET_BASELINE` plus a\n`test_any_ratchet_strict_set_only_grows` mirroring the existing subset assertion, so the\n`Any` tier can only ever grow. `disallow_any_explicit` is added to the existing\n`_DEFERRED_GLOBAL_FLAGS`-style check as an override-only flag (never a global key).\n\n**E. Record it in `docs/architecture.md`** (\"mypy strictness ratchet\" section): that\n`disallow_untyped_defs` is satisfied by `: Any` and therefore delivers neither driver, the\ntwo-tier ratchet (untyped-def tier + explicit-`Any` tier), and the measured\nbefore/after table above as the baseline the tiers shrink from.\n\n## Explicitly OUT of scope -> `discovered_from` follow-ups filed before close\n\n- `llm` / `_commands` / `_engine` annotation + `Any` reduction (573 untyped defs, ~389\n  explicit `Any`) — epic-sized, and `llm/pass1.py` is at the module-size cap.\n- The reconciler transport port converted end-to-end with a Serena reference-finding\n  measurement (already scoped by `cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8`; blocked on the same near-cap\n  files).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n(Refined at planning time; supersedes the provisional list in the original filing.)\n\n- [x] `mypy src/rebar/<pkg> --disallow-untyped-defs` is clean for all promoted packages, and\n      `pyproject.toml` lists them in the `disallow_untyped_defs` override (2 before, **13**\n      after — `reducer` was dropped from the planned 14; see the deviation comment and\n      follow-up d893-e003-0539-47fc).\n- [x] A second `[[tool.mypy.overrides]]` block sets `disallow_any_explicit = true` for\n      `rebar._cli.*` and `rebar._snapshot.*`, and\n      `mypy src/rebar/_cli src/rebar/_snapshot --disallow-untyped-defs --disallow-any-explicit`\n      is clean — i.e. the ratchet now constrains `Any`, not only unannotated defs.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py` pins BOTH tiers as shrink-only (removing any\n      package from either list turns the build red), verified by running the test.\n- [x] The annotation work adds **no new `: Any` / `-> Any`**, machine-checked with an\n      asserting command (same oracle sibling 9efe used):\n      `test \"$(grep -rhoE ':[[:space:]]*Any\\b|->[[:space:]]*Any\\b' src/rebar --include='*.py' | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\" = \"$BASELINE\"`\n      exits 0, where `$BASELINE` is the count captured on `origin/main` before the change.\n- [x] `docs/architecture.md` records the `Any`-blindness of `disallow_untyped_defs`, the\n      two-tier ratchet, and the measured per-package baseline table.\n- [x] Full local gate set green (ten `check_*` gates, generators no-diff, `make lint`,\n      `make typecheck`, CI pytest selection, `tests/integration`), and the change lands\n      `Verified +1` / `LLM-Review +1`.\n- [x] Follow-up tickets filed and linked `discovered_from` for the two out-of-scope items.\n\n## Result (measured)\n\n- Ratchet **tier 1** (`disallow_untyped_defs`): 2 → **13** packages (`_cli`, `_engine_support`,\n  `_io`, `_snapshot`, `_store`, `attest`, `audit`, `graph`, `grounding`, `metrics`,\n  `opcert_service`, `review_bot`, `schemas`). 36 defs annotated.\n- Ratchet **tier 2** (`disallow_any_explicit`, NEW): `rebar._cli.*`, `rebar._snapshot.*`.\n- Repo-wide explicit-`Any` count **unchanged** (no new `Any` introduced).\n- Gates: `make lint`, `make typecheck` (527 files), `make config-check`, complexity baseline,\n  all `check_*` scripts, generators no-diff; local suite **12835 passed**; `tests/integration`\n  **194 passed, 1 skipped**.\n- Landed as Gerrit change 1735 → `c389e4c8b9` on `origin/main` (`LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"promote 12 already-clean packages into the disallow_untyped_defs ratchet and add the disallow_any_explicit tier"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py","reason":"pin both ratchet tiers as shrink-only"},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"record that disallow_untyped_defs is satisfied by Any, the two-tier ratchet, and the measured baseline"},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/cache.py","reason":"annotate open_in_snapshot return type"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/hlc.py","reason":"annotate _hlc_lock return type"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_filters.py","reason":"annotate match_predicate value param"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py","reason":"annotate registry/validator return types"},{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/jobs.py","reason":"annotate run_job and the _dispatch_* callback params"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py","reason":"annotate repo_root params"},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py","reason":"annotate repo_root param"},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/export_ndjson.py","reason":"annotate repo_root param"},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/_cli.py","reason":"annotate repo_root params"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/output.py","reason":"annotate _resolve_profile and error_envelope"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py","reason":"annotate _load_classify return type"},{"path":"src/rebar/audit/read.py","reason":"annotate repo_root params"},{"path":"src/rebar/audit/server.py","reason":"annotate _render_ticket params"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py","reason":"annotate argparse Namespace params"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_workflow_commands.py","reason":"annotate argparse Namespace params"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"annotate _ref_lock_module return type"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07"],["relates_to","9c4c-a2d9-1604-4fe1"],["relates_to","9efe-8e88-70b3-4984"],["relates_to","ae1b-b2a0-a080-4b4e"],["relates_to","cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8"],["relates_to","dbf9-3fc8-625d-4730"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07","parent_status_uuid":"595755c1-f6de-46c2-b3f2-609d845aa9c9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"06e0-fb68-657a-4ea1","ticket_type":"story","title":"Ratchet Any and loose typing repo-wide: typed contracts for navigability and testability","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ba977e23-d35a-489f-a9b2-f11682097dd8","46f8d3bd-e094-49fe-8a4b-bfd0b8a255de","9d6eb8ab-731d-4bf3-9bce-97620d874e6d","d331b329-c360-440b-8c79-9bb7639adea1","f6117b42-6ae6-42eb-bb6d-1069320664a3","62276737-8d4b-4e90-b669-5bd0bc8c20bf","6bc57fab-6936-4c97-a342-1fc23f30e791","80b9dc6e-bc5f-4889-9fac-3b755579d5d0","fdab6fff-cd81-4799-82e0-9ca6ac45d184","88ed1f9d-3a3d-453e-97c2-06c91caf6d02","c52b7afe-ac8e-40bc-9d15-e4f5c8adca78","c9cc772b-ce59-45fb-a87f-dd606acc3ec5","18ce7297-6348-4e4f-a179-c166a273ccad","f28f8f35-95fc-40bd-8a9b-9b35fe917437","881dea18-a1a0-4f54-8ec0-5c9213a9ea3e","c490904c-e2f2-4a03-a2a9-04381a33a345","7daa3a39-65a3-457f-95a1-d3118739230c","595755c1-f6de-46c2-b3f2-609d845aa9c9","dd114504-ffb3-42a9-865f-770854143a0d"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786666592626433091,"uuid":"18ced433-154d-4d2b-b1f8-4795c55dfc95"}